A||N||4||perks88gt||RYAN/HELD suspension...||||1||
Z||000000||perks88gt||08-09-2001||07:24 PM||||I have been considering purchasing the HELD (formely ryan) motor sports suspension package for my 88 gt.  I am going for the whole bang, tubulars, coil-overs, rear end links, etc.  I was wondering if anyone has experience with there suspension setups?  Is it worth $1700.00  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||pherder||08-09-2001||08:45 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by perks88gt:<BR><B>I have been considering purchasing the HELD (formely ryan) motor sports suspension package for my 88 gt.  I am going for the whole bang, tubulars, coil-overs, rear end links, etc.  I was wondering if anyone has experience with there suspension setups?  Is it worth $1700.00  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, I don't see how you got your $1700 figure?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>The front end tubular control arms with coil over shocks is $900<P>The upper tubular control arms are $396.<P>You don't get ball joints with them (you do get poly bushings) so add another ~ $236 to the cost (The Fiero Store prices) or $1532 just for the front end.<P>Add new upper control arm shafts (you are putting all new arms on so why not add new control shafts from The Fiero Store) @ ~$160 for a pair.  <P>Now your total is up to $1692 before shipping/etc.<P>And that is <B>JUST</B> for the front end!<P>Add $618 for the rear links (2 radius arms, 2 lateral links and 2 toe links) and ~$465 for the cheapest (KYB) coil over struts (assembled ... not the kit) and I come up with a total of $1083 for the rear.<P>The total for the front and rear that I come up with is <B>$2775!!!</B><P>I have all the above names pieces <B>EXCEPT</B> for the 6 rear links <B>AND</B> I have the Bilstein coil over struts for the rear instead of the KYBs.  Held and The Fiero Store gets $2460 for them, new, unassembled.  Mine have the ball joints mounted (bolted on the upper arms and pressed into the lower arms).  The rear struts have been mounted on to one of my 88s BUT was never driven with them on (took them off the one car to use on another 88 I had).  <P>I would sell all the above in one package (i.e. I am <B>NOT</B> interested in splitting it up so don't ask!) for $2000 (USD) plus actual costs to UPS it to you.<P>Well, I would separate front from rear and sell the front end pieces for $1500 and the rear Bilsteins for $500.<P>Reason I would sell ... been unemployed for going on 4 months now.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I do have a kit car (an Artero) that I am putting on an 88 Formula doner that I could use these parts on BUT the kit does not require lowering to look right so these pieces are "extra".  <P>Again, the front end pieces have never been mounted on a car, the rear struts have but only to see how they would fit on the car before I changed my mine on which car they were going to be used on.<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||08-09-2001||08:48 PM||||twodmax@hotmail.com <P>this is George Ryans Email. Anyone who races Fiero's knows him. He had a A- Prepared (SCCA Lingo) coupe , weighed 1900lbs and had a 240hp quad 4<P>I don't wanna bash vendors , but I believe he has had the setup your looking at. Note I said HAD..<P>He is a great guy and will help you on your way to getting your fiero to really handle.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||08-09-2001||09:08 PM||||Jonathan,<P>Let's compare apples to apples.  George had a problem with the 84-87 sport front end suspension on his 84 race car.<P>He was using the Ryane 88 to earlier frame conversion (i.e. mounting the 88 rear cradle to the 84-87 Fiero) in the rear and loved it!<P>We are talking about the 88s.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000004||perks88gt||08-10-2001||01:39 AM||||Well thanks for the pricing input, I got that quote from HELD.  But im looking for first hand experience, how did it ride?  Was the handling good?  Is it that much better than stock 88' suspension?  Has anyone realy used this suspension?||||reg||1
